{
  // Fresh Codespaces ship without Pillow, so scripts/generate_og.py,
  // generate_project_card.py, and generate_site_og.py all die on
  // "No module named 'PIL'" until it's installed by hand. CI already installs
  // it in build-og.yml; this does the same for the editor, and fetches the
  // brand fonts so a card rendered locally matches one rendered in CI.
  //
  // qrcode added 2026-08-11 for scripts/generate_contact_card.py. Named
  // separately rather than as qrcode[pil], so the two reasons Pillow is here
  // stay visible: the OG renderers need it on its own account, and dropping
  // the contact card later should not silently take Pillow with it.
  //
  // beautifulsoup4 and lxml added 2026-08-31, and the reason is worth writing
  // down. scripts/build_feed.py imports bs4 and parses with the lxml backend
  // explicitly, so it cannot start without both; it is the sole generator of
  // feed.xml, blog/index.html, sitemap.xml, and robots.txt. build-feed.yml
  // installs them, this file never did, and a hand-run in a Codespace worked
  // anyway — because the publishing agent's own requirements.txt happened to
  // carry bs4 and lxml, and installing it in the same Codespace covered the
  // gap. Nothing in that repo imports either package; they were leftovers, and
  // removing them there is what exposed this. Same shape as the BLOG_REPO bug
  // in that repo's agent.py: a dependency that looked configured because an
  // unrelated default happened to satisfy it. Declared here on its own account
  // now, so the editor environment stands up without borrowing from a
  // neighbouring repo.
  "name": "rnvizion.github.io",
  "image": "mcr.microsoft.com/devcontainers/universal:2",
  "postCreateCommand": "pip install --user Pillow qrcode beautifulsoup4 lxml && bash scripts/font.sh",
  "customizations": {
    "vscode": {
      "extensions": [
        "ms-python.python"
      ]
    }
  }
}
